   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1): APPROVE** — head 5620ee6854b9f87d3eb468d2a9008d84960b2d5d\n\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Settings/ThemedListTests.swift:342-357`: `aSelectedRowAndASectionUnderTheListLookFollowTheTheme` only runs the classic look (the `listLook` default). #1125 item 2 asks to extend `theListLookRowsFollowTheThemeInBothLooks`. The risky case is the dense look: the outer `listLookRows()` sets the row clear and the inner `listLookRow(isSelected: true)` must still paint `selection`. If precedence breaks there, a dense themed list loses its selection and this test stays green. Fix: loop over `[.classic, .dense]` as the title test does, and check that the unselected row is `surface` in classic and black in dense.\n2. **Detail**, `ThemedListTests.swift:352`: the comment says \"centres at about 100 + header, 300 + header, 500 + header\", but the list has two rows. The probes at y 150 and 350 do fall inside rows 1 and 2 as long as the top margin plus the header stays under 150 pt. Fix: describe two rows.\n\nNo other findings:\n- The precedence is sound. The inner `listLookTitleRow()` clear background wins over the outer `themedListRow` surface.\n- Legacy is unchanged, because `listColors` is nil.\n- Same-file `private` access and `@MainActor` isolation both carry over to the extension, and `@Test` works in an extension of a suite.\n- The new pairs match what the dense look draws. Their rows have no `meta` or `counter`.\n- Bookmarks (`BookmarksView.swift:70`) now goes through `listLookRow`, so the new test covers it.\n\nVerified: `swift test --filter Theme` (HFRKit) at the head, 24 passed; `swiftlint` clean on the four Swift files; new pairs on `background` ≥ 5.85:1 on the bundled `noel-abuse` and the `test-theme` fixture. The hosted tests could not be run on Linux.\n\nAuthor response: both findings fixed in one commit (both looks, two-row comment); test-only change, hosted tests still owed by the Compile check.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
